  {
   "id": 520441,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure><img src=\"exercises/media/8c3e132676426b28.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Brown, et al./<i>American Journal of Physiology</i>)\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the core body temperature and metabolic rate during hibernation for a ground squirrel  measured over 1 month.</p>\n<p>What is a scientific claim that can be done using this data?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1017169,
     "content_html": "Ground squirrels hibernate without interruption."
    },
    {
     "id": 1017170,
     "content_html": "During hibernation, ground squirrels wake up once every week."
    },
    {
     "id": 1017171,
     "content_html": "During hibernation, ground squirrels wake up twice a month."
    },
    {
     "id": 1017172,
     "content_html": "During hibernation, ground squirrels wake up once every ten days."
    }
   ],
